      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on tenant mix, pricing strategy, and owner expectations for launch.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 349749,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, welcome to the official channel for the mixed-use property launch. Our first critical milestone is to finalize the leasing strategy. The goal is to lock down the target tenant mix and initial pricing this week for owner sign-off. This is our main focus for T1.",
            "mentions": [
              286305,
              316072,
              518065,
              526084
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 349749,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "To get us started, I've created the 12-Month Financial Forecast draft in A4 and the Unit Inventory tracker in A1. Please review them when you have a moment.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 286305,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Thanks. I've already done a competitive analysis of three similar local properties. My initial recommendation is a 70/30 residential to commercial split to capitalize on the current high demand for apartments. This mix should help us hit occupancy targets faster.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "👍",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 518065,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "That makes sense. For the commercial units, are we thinking more about retail on the ground floor and offices on the second, or a mix? The type of tenant will affect our marketing.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 286305,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Good question. I suggest we prioritize low-fit-out tenants for speed: small professional services, boutique shops, maybe a cafe. We can hold one larger unit for a higher-value tenant that might require more work.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "💯",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 349749,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "I agree. Minimizing initial fit-out costs and delays is key. So, a 70/30 residential/commercial split, with a focus on low-impact commercial tenants. Let's make that our official target mix.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 526084,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Sorry, where is the unit list located?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 286305,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "It's in the Unit Inventory and Availability Tracker, which is artifact A1. I can ping you the direct link.",
            "mentions": [
              526084
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 316072,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "The 70/30 split sounds good to me.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "👍",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 349749,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "Great. Now for pricing. @286305 what are your thoughts on initial bands and potential promotions?",
            "mentions": [
              286305
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 286305,
            "reply_to": "M10",
            "text": "Based on my market analysis, I've added suggested pricing bands to the forecast in A4. I also modeled a 'first month free' promotion for the first 5 residential leases signed. It's an aggressive move but should create immediate buzz and momentum.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 518065,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "I like the promo idea. It's a clear, simple offer. Does the forecast in A4 account for that initial dip in revenue?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
            "speaker_id": 286305,
            "reply_to": "M12",
            "text": "Yes, it's factored into the 'base' and 'optimistic' scenarios. The impact on annual revenue is minimal if it helps us lease up faster, which I'm confident it will.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M14",
            "speaker_id": 349749,
            "reply_to": "M13",
            "text": "Excellent work. The data supports the decision. Let's approve the pricing bands as listed in A4, including the 'first month free' promo for the first 5 residential leases.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "🚀",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M15",
            "speaker_id": 526084,
            "reply_to": "M14",
            "text": "ok, i agree with the pricing.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M16",
            "speaker_id": 316072,
            "reply_to": "M14",
            "text": "The plan is approved.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M17",
            "speaker_id": 349749,
            "reply_to": "M14",
            "text": "Perfect. That closes T1. I will document these decisions for the owner. @286305, please update A1 with the final pricing.",
            "mentions": [
              286305
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
