      {
        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Ensure building readiness, safety compliance, and coordination with construction.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 349749,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Morning all. I just completed a site walk-through with the construction manager. I've updated the Pre-Launch Snagging and Safety Readiness Checklist (A5). There are a number of items, particularly in common areas, that need to be addressed before we can allow any tenant move-ins. This is critical for T5.",
            "mentions": [
              286305,
              518065,
              316072,
              526084
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 286305,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "Thanks for the update. Are any of the residential units affected? I have prospective tenants scheduled for viewings later this week.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 349749,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "The units themselves are mostly fine, but access routes and the main lobby have pending items. We can't show the property if the first impression is a construction zone. We need to prioritize.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 518065,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "Looking at A5, I see items like 'pending fire safety certification' and 'emergency lighting test incomplete'. These are absolute blockers for occupancy from a safety and compliance standpoint.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "⚠️",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 349749,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "Exactly. I've already communicated this to the construction team. Here is the priority I propose: P0 for all life-safety systems. P1 for common area access and presentation. P2 for minor cosmetic defects within units. All P0 items must be cleared before any other clock starts. This is our official priority list.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 526084,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "I hope the construction team can get it all done. It seems like a lot of work left.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 349749,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "I am tracking their progress daily. The risk of delay is high, but we are managing it actively. Now, let's shift to T7. The draft Building Health, Safety, and Emergency Procedures are in A6. @518065, given your experience with safety planning, could you please take the lead on reviewing this?",
            "mentions": [
              518065
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T7",
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 518065,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "Of course. I'll review A6 today and ensure it aligns with all building and fire codes. I'll add comments directly in the document.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 286305,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "Once A6 is finalized, we should create a one-page summary of emergency procedures for the tenant welcome pack. Something clear and easy to understand.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "💡",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 349749,
            "reply_to": "M45",
            "text": "Excellent idea. Let's add that to the list of deliverables for the onboarding process.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 316072,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "The safety procedures are very important.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 518065,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Update: I've completed my review of A6 and added a section for on-site staff roles during an emergency. It's ready for final approval.",
            "mentions": [],
